    "cluster": "Platform Architecture",
    "question": "~~**Which specific encrypted-session-cookie mechanism/library** (e.g. `iron-session`, a hand-rolled JWE via `jose`, or Next.js's own newer built-in session primitives if available at implementation time) — left to Story 6.1's own implementation, not decided here; the requirement is the property (httpOnly, encrypted, never client-JS-readable), not a specific library.~~ — **resolved 2026-08-04:** a hand-rolled JWE via `jose` (consistent with `entraAuthMiddleware.ts`'s existing use of `jose` on the core side), but not encrypting the tokens directly into the cookie as first built — a real, verified constraint this ADR didn't anticipate: Entra CIAM's real `id_token`+`access_token`+`refresh_token` together exceed the ~4KB per-cookie limit browsers enforce, and a browser silently drops an oversized `Set-Cookie` rather than erroring. The cookie instead holds a small encrypted `{ sid }` reference into an in-memory, server-side session store — itself a named instance of this ADR's own \"a reference/session-ID pattern, OR an encrypted-cookie session store\" alternative (§1), not a departure from it. See `social-listening-admin/.claude/skills/admin-auth-session/SKILL.md`'s own \"Load-bearing constraints.\"",
    "status": "RESOLVED",
