    "question": "**Whether Blob-Storage-tier deletion is itself verifiably complete** (e.g., confirming no soft-delete/versioning retention on the storage account would silently preserve a \"deleted\" blob) — a real implementation-verification step for whoever builds this, not designed here. **Pending supersession note, added 2026-08-06 — narrower supersession, since superseded by the note below.** [ADR-0043](0043-self-service-tenant-initiated-deletion.md) was originally drafted to supersede only this section's \"A tenant cannot self-delete its own account via any self-service mechanism\" sentence, leaving Decision §1's \"Platform-Admin-initiated only\" framing itself intact as an additional, parallel path. That narrower framing has itself since been superseded — see the note immediately below. **Superseding note, added 2026-08-07 — in effect once ADR-0043 (as amended the same date) is accepted.** Story 3.7 was built the night of 2026-08-06/07 exactly as this ADR's Decision §1 originally specified: `platform_admin_role`-gated, `POST /v1/admin/tenants/:id/export` / `.../delete`. Running the full contract suite surfaced that this directly contradicts Story 5.7's own already-accepted \"platform_admin_role has zero access to tenant-content tables\" boundary (ADR-0030 §2) — satisfying Decision §1 required a real, if narrow, widening of that boundary (migrations/0023). Menno reviewed this collision directly and corrected the decision, verbatim: *\"platform admin cannot touch update delete tenant admin information so that contract stands strong now failing... Story 3.7 should have drafted that only a tenant admin delete it own data\"* and, on the question of whether both paths should coexist as originally designed here and in ADR-0043: *\"I am very sure we agreed that the tenant admin does so on self service deletion that the platform admin does not interfere.\"* **This supersedes Decision §1 in full, not only its \"cannot self-delete\" sentence**: there is no Platform-Admin-initiated deletion path. Tenant deletion is `tenant_admin`-initiated only, own-tenant-only, per ADR-0043 (as amended 2026-08-07) — the mechanism ADR-0043 already designed (export, grace period, confirm) becomes the *only* deletion trigger, not a second, additive one alongside Story 3.7's Platform-Admin routes. Story 3.7's originally-built Platform-Admin-gated routes and migration 0023's `platform_admin_role` grants are retired as part of this same correction, before ever being committed. **No other part of this ADR's Decision or Consequences text is affected** — ADR-0043 continues to reuse Decision §2 (export scope), §3 (per-table deletion treatment), §4 (async/bounded execution), and §5 (suspension distinct from deletion) exactly as decided here; only *who* triggers the mechanism changes, not what the mechanism itself does.",
