    "adrFile": "0060-facebook-connector-multiple-pages-per-user.md",
    "cluster": "Platform Architecture",
    "question": "**`RequestGate`'s `(tenantId, providerId)` keying does not account for per-Page or per-user call volume** — a real, concrete risk once one user's poll cycle fans out across many Pages, worse still if multiple users each connect several Pages under the same tenant. Sequential per-Page polling (Decision §3, added at review) mitigates the burst/concurrency shape of this risk by reusing `RequestGate`'s own existing serialization — it does not mitigate the shared-budget-division shape (more callers drawing from one still-flat, still-placeholder ceiling). Not redesigned here; needs its own follow-up (possibly a Story-time addition, possibly its own ADR if the fix turns out to be structural, e.g. keying by `(tenantId, providerId, userId)`) — deliberately not pre-emptively built, since no real, measured fan-out volume yet demonstrates the shared budget is actually insufficient, the same \"don't invent a fix for an unmeasured need\" discipline ADR-0057 Decision §3 already applied to feed-count caps. **Note:** an external review round (see Amendment Log) additionally claimed this fan-out would trigger Meta's specific \"Error Code 4 (Application request limit reached)\" — that specific claim is not primary-source-verified against `developers.facebook.com` in this session and is recorded here as unconfirmed, not asserted as fact anywhere in this ADR's own Decision text, per this project's own ADR-0059 verification bar.",
